<title>UKRAINE: Ukraine grain harvest behind 1996 levels.</title>
<headline>Ukraine grain harvest behind 1996 levels.</headline>
<dateline>KIEV 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ukraine has harvested 9.18 million tonnes of grain this year, down from 13.49 million tonnes at this time last year, the Statistics Ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Crop yields were 2.87 tonnes per hectare against 2.12 tonnes in the same period in 1996, a ministry statement said.</p>
<p>Ukrainian officials last week revised upward the grain harvest forecast to 37 million tonnes from 35 million tonnes, Interfax news agency reported.</p>
<p>The 1996 drought-hit grain harvest was 25.4 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The Statistics Ministry gave the following data on harvest progress:</p>
<p>				   July 28 1997    July 28 1996</p>
<p> Cut (million hectares)	  4.25		6.95</p>
<p> Threshed (million tonnes)     9.18		13.49</p>
<p> Yields (tonnes/hectare)	 2.87		2.12</p>
<p>--Irene Marushko, Kiev Newsroom +380 44 244-9150</p>
</text>
